Serve required attributes first and cap optional ones at half the slots.

Every attribute holds a global build slot while it runs, including a
best-effort (ignoreFailure) one waiting on a remote builder. During a
nixpkgs bump the darwin attributes held all 16 slots for hours, so the
required x86_64-linux attributes never started and the grace that stops
optional attributes never armed. The pool now serves required waiters
before optional ones and lets optional jobs hold at most half the slots
(at least one).

